@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n08. Historical Explanation and Audit | UC-25..26
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #FFF0ED
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "user : AuthorizedUser/Auditor" as User <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "query : EvidenceQueryService" as Query
object "hot : HotTraceStore" as Hot
object "ledger : ComplianceLedger" as Ledger
object "audit : AuditEvidence" as Audit
User --> API : 1: explain(executionId) / inspectAudit(filter)
API --> Auth : 1.1: authorize evidence action and scope
API --> Query : 1.2 [authorized]: query within Tenant/Workspace
Query --> Hot : 1.2.1a [explain]: find retained protected tree
Query --> Ledger : 1.2.2a [explain]: find retained execution metadata
Query --> Audit : 1.2.3a [explain and accessible reference]: read release evidence\n1.2.1b [inspect]: read scoped governance/deployment/security evidence
Query --> Query : 1.2.4: assemble authorized retained evidence
Query --> Audit : 1.2.5: record evidence access actor, scope, query and time
API ..> User : 1.3: protected evidence / unavailable / access denied
note bottom of Query
Paths a (explain) and b (inspect) are alternatives.
Expired full trace: return retained metadata with explicit limitation.
Do not invent missing intermediate outcomes.
Denied scope returns no evidence and discloses no resource contents.
end note
legend bottom
  Sequence numbers identify message order, not spatial position.
  Nested numbers identify calls; routine returns are omitted.
  [condition] guards a message; ..> is the displayed response.
endlegend
@enduml
